# {{.Name}}

A Sora theme extension — a theme is data, not code.

> **Status: contract per `reports/extensions-40/spec-theme-runtime.md`.**
> The manifest side is real; the app-side theme engine is not implemented
> yet. Deliberately **no CSS**: CSS is an executable surface (`url()` →
> exfiltration, `@import` → network), so the engine only accepts validated
> tokens.

## theme.json

- `theme_version: 1`, `name`
- `tokens`: `color.*` (`#rgb`/`#rrggbb`/`#rrggbbaa`, `transparent`),
  `radius.*` (0..32), `font.scale` (0.8..1.3), `opacity.*` (0..1).
  Unknown token names are rejected, not ignored.
- `dark.tokens` (optional): overrides for dark brightness.
- Contrast gate: every `onX`/`X` pair must pass WCAG AA (4.5:1) or the
  theme is refused with the reason in the extension log.

Applying is atomic; disabling the extension restores the system theme.
The `theme.apply` permission is sensitive, and installing never
auto-applies the theme.

## Ship

```sh
sora-ext validate
sora-ext pack . -o {{.ID}}.soraext
sora-ext sign --key author.key {{.ID}}.soraext
```
